    <h1>About LienForm</h1>

    <p class="lead">LienForm is a free mechanics lien document generator for contractors, subcontractors, and material suppliers working on US construction projects.</p>

    <h2>What We Do</h2>
    <p>When a contractor or supplier doesn't get paid for work on a construction project, a mechanics lien is one of the most powerful tools available. Filing a lien attaches a legal claim to the property title — the owner can't sell or refinance until the debt is resolved.</p>
    <p>LienForm makes it straightforward to generate a legally correct lien document bundle. You enter your project details, we generate the complete set of documents pre-filled with your information and the correct statutory citation for your state.</p>

    <h2>Why We Built It</h2>
    <p>Most mechanics lien templates online cite outdated statutes. California's old §3082 was repealed in 2012 — competitors still cite it. Texas updated its monthly notice requirements via HB 2237 in 2022 — most templates don't reflect this. Michigan amended the Construction Lien Act in 2023 — old forms are wrong.</p>
    <p>LienForm was built to close that gap: current law, correct citations, role-aware deadlines, and county-specific filing guidance — in one place.</p>

    <h2>What's Included in Every Bundle</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Mechanics Lien Claim with current statutory citation</li>
      <li>Deadline Confirmation — your exact filing deadline with days remaining</li>
      <li>County Recorder / Clerk Filing Instructions</li>
      <li>Proof of Service Affidavit</li>
      <li>Lien Release Form</li>
      <li>Preliminary Notice (auto-included for California and Florida subcontractors)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Early Access</h2>
    <p>LienForm is currently in early access. We're building out coverage for all 50 states. Michigan, California, Texas, and Florida (Notice to Owner) are live. More states are added regularly.</p>
    <p>The service is free during early access. Pricing may be introduced in the future.</p>

    <h2>Important Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>LienForm is not a law firm and does not provide legal advice. Documents generated are for informational purposes only. Please consult a licensed attorney in your state before filing a lien.</p>

    <h2>Get in Touch</h2>
    <p>Questions or feedback? <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a>.</p>
